// Checked in. DEVELOPMENT_TEAM defaults to empty so a fresh clone never needs a real
// team id — most CI builds use CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO and don't need one either; the
// signed RC/TestFlight builds write a real value into Local.xcconfig at build time from
// a secret (see release.yml/promote-testflight.yml), same mechanism as local dev.
//
// CODE_SIGN_STYLE defaults to Automatic (the previous pbxproj-hardcoded value, moved
// here so it stays a default rather than fixed — same reason DEVELOPMENT_TEAM lives
// here and not directly in buildSettings: a direct pbxproj entry always wins over an
// xcconfig value, so it has to live here for Local.xcconfig to be able to override it.
// The signed RC/TestFlight builds override it to Manual + a named distribution profile
// (see release.yml/promote-testflight.yml) — confirmed the hard way that leaving the
// hardcoded Automatic in the pbxproj causes "conflicting provisioning settings" once a
// provisioning profile is specified from the CI xcconfig.
//
// #include? is optional — it silently no-ops when Local.xcconfig doesn't exist.
// See Local.xcconfig.example.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
